# Ledger row actions

This project uses Base UI, not Radix `asChild`. Nesting `DropdownMenuTrigger` around `Button` creates two buttons and drops click handlers.

- Trigger must be **one** native button. Style it with `buttonVariants`; do not `render={<Button />}`.
- Portal once to `document.body` at `z-[9999]`. Do not wrap `DropdownMenuContent` in a second portal.
- Stop click/pointer propagation on the trigger so table cells cannot swallow the event.
- Edit items must call the parent `onEdit(row)` that sets selected project + opens the modal.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — nested interactive hosts, dead clicks
<DropdownMenuTrigger render={<Button />}>...</DropdownMenuTrigger>

// ✅ GOOD
<DropdownMenuTrigger
  type="button"
  className={cn(buttonVariants({ variant: "ghost" }), "h-8 w-8 p-0")}
  onClick={(event) => event.stopPropagation()}
>
  <MoreHorizontal />
</DropdownMenuTrigger>
```
